cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Weight-Space Index (wsi) or Mixture of Indexes (MoI), please cite it as below."
title: "Weight-Space Index (wsi) and Mixture of Indexes (MoI)"
abstract: >-
  Weight-Space Index (wsi) indexes the circuits of a transformer directly from its weights.
  Mixture of Indexes (MoI) uses those indexes to change what a model loads or runs depending on the task.
  Additive MoI keeps every weight and switches small weight edits on only when a router detects that they are
  needed (for example, a reasoning-loop fix that WSI discovers from the base model alone).
  Compensated Selective MoI loads only a task's subset of MLP neurons and refits the kept down-projection
  columns from about 20k calibration tokens, which yields smaller and faster real checkpoints.
